IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg2-support`
IMPORT `dg2-board-committees`

-- Tests of dg2-board-committees.l4 (8 Del. C. section 141(c)). Expected values are written by hand from src:365 to src:368 of
-- de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt, beside each assertion, before the run.

§ `Which paragraph governs`

-- src:365: before 1 July 1996 paragraph (c)(1) governs, unless a majority of the whole board elected (c)(2); on or after, (c)(2).
#ASSERT `s 141(c) which paragraph governs the corporation` (YMD 1996 6 30) 9 NOTHING EQUALS JUST `paragraph (c)(1) of section 141 governs the corporation`
#ASSERT `s 141(c) which paragraph governs the corporation` (YMD 1996 7 1) 9 NOTHING EQUALS JUST `paragraph (c)(2) of section 141 governs the corporation`
#ASSERT `s 141(c) which paragraph governs the corporation` (YMD 2020 1 1) 9 NOTHING EQUALS JUST `paragraph (c)(2) of section 141 governs the corporation`
-- A resolution of a majority of the whole board (5 of 9) elects (c)(2); 4 of 9 does not.
#ASSERT `s 141(c) which paragraph governs the corporation` (YMD 1995 1 1) 9 (JUST 5) EQUALS JUST `paragraph (c)(2) of section 141 governs the corporation`
#ASSERT `s 141(c) which paragraph governs the corporation` (YMD 1995 1 1) 9 (JUST 4) EQUALS JUST `paragraph (c)(1) of section 141 governs the corporation`
-- 4 of 8 is half, not a majority.
#ASSERT `s 141(c) which paragraph governs the corporation` (YMD 1995 1 1) 8 (JUST 4) EQUALS JUST `paragraph (c)(1) of section 141 governs the corporation`
#ASSERT `s 141(c) which paragraph governs the corporation` (YMD 1995 1 1) 8 (JUST 5) EQUALS JUST `paragraph (c)(2) of section 141 governs the corporation`
-- More votes than seats cannot be a vote: not covered.
#ASSERT `s 141(c) which paragraph governs the corporation` (YMD 1995 1 1) 9 (JUST 10) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A corporation incorporated on or after 1 July 1996 is under (c)(2) whatever a resolution says.
#ASSERT `s 141(c) which paragraph governs the corporation` (YMD 1997 1 1) 9 (JUST 2) EQUALS JUST `paragraph (c)(2) of section 141 governs the corporation`

§ `Designating committees, alternates, replacements`

-- (c)(1) src:365: resolution passed by a majority of the whole board (5 of 9); a committee of 1 or more directors.
#ASSERT `s 141(c)(1) the board may designate the committee` 9 5 2 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 141(c)(1) the board may designate the committee` 9 4 2 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 141(c)(1) the board may designate the committee` 9 5 1 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 141(c)(1) the board may designate the committee` 9 5 0 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 141(c)(1) the board may designate the committee` 9 5 2 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A vote that cannot be a vote is not covered, unless the committee itself is already invalid (then FALSE whatever the vote).
#ASSERT `s 141(c)(1) the board may designate the committee` 9 10 2 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 141(c)(1) the board may designate the committee` 9 10 0 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (c)(2) src:366: no vote is stated, so the board's act under s 141(b) suffices; a committee of 1 or more directors.
#ASSERT `s 141(c)(2) the board may designate the committee` TRUE 2 TRUE
#ASSERT `s 141(c)(2) the board may designate the committee` TRUE 1 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 141(c)(2) the board may designate the committee` FALSE 2 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 141(c)(2) the board may designate the committee` TRUE 0 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 141(c)(2) the board may designate the committee` TRUE 2 FALSE

-- src:365-366: alternates designated by the board, directors, replace an absent or disqualified member.
#ASSERT `s 141(c) an alternate member may replace the member at the meeting` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 141(c) an alternate member may replace the member at the meeting` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 141(c) an alternate member may replace the member at the meeting` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 141(c) an alternate member may replace the member at the meeting` TRUE TRUE FALSE

-- src:365-366: the bylaws may let the members present unanimously appoint another director in place of an absent member.
#ASSERT `s 141(c) the members present may appoint another director to act in place of the absent member` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 141(c) the members present may appoint another director to act in place of the absent member` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 141(c) the members present may appoint another director to act in place of the absent member` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 141(c) the members present may appoint another director to act in place of the absent member` TRUE TRUE FALSE

§ `What a committee may do`

-- a grant: (the resolution or bylaws give the committee the board's power, the instrument expressly so provides, the committee acts
-- to the extent authorized by the s 151(a) resolution, this chapter requires the matter to go to stockholders).
GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 141(c) What the board or the bylaws gave the committee`
`a grant` a b c d MEANS `s 141(c) What the board or the bylaws gave the committee` WITH
    `the resolution of the board of directors or the bylaws provide that the committee has and may exercise the power of the board` IS a
    `the resolution, the bylaws or the certificate of incorporation expressly provide that the committee may do the thing` IS b
    `the committee acts to the extent authorized in a resolution providing for the issuance of shares adopted by the board as provided in s 151(a)` IS c
    `this chapter expressly requires the matter to be submitted to stockholders for approval` IS d

-- (c)(1) src:365: no power to amend the certificate, adopt a listed merger, recommend a sale of all assets or a dissolution, or amend the bylaws.
#ASSERT `s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `paragraph (c)(1) of section 141 governs the corporation` `amending the certificate of incorporation, otherwise than by fixing the terms of shares under a resolution adopted as provided in s 151(a)` (`a grant` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `paragraph (c)(1) of section 141 governs the corporation` `adopting an agreement of merger or consolidation under s 251, 252, 254, 255, 256, 257, 258, 263 or 264` (`a grant` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `paragraph (c)(1) of section 141 governs the corporation` `recommending to the stockholders the sale, lease or exchange of all or substantially all of the corporation's property and assets` (`a grant` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `paragraph (c)(1) of section 141 governs the corporation` `recommending to the stockholders a dissolution of the corporation or a revocation of a dissolution` (`a grant` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `paragraph (c)(1) of section 141 governs the corporation` `amending a bylaw of the corporation` (`a grant` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (c)(1) names only "amending" the bylaws; whether a committee may adopt or repeal one it does not say.
#ASSERT `s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `paragraph (c)(1) of section 141 governs the corporation` `adopting a bylaw of the corporation` (`a grant` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `paragraph (c)(1) of section 141 governs the corporation` `repealing a bylaw of the corporation` (`a grant` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The exception: fix the terms of shares, or the number of shares of a series, to the extent the s 151(a) resolution authorizes.
#ASSERT `s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `paragraph (c)(1) of section 141 governs the corporation` `fixing the designations and preferences or rights of shares, or the number of shares of a series, or authorizing an increase or decrease in them, under a resolution adopted by the board as provided in s 151(a)` (`a grant` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `paragraph (c)(1) of section 141 governs the corporation` `fixing the designations and preferences or rights of shares, or the number of shares of a series, or authorizing an increase or decrease in them, under a resolution adopted by the board as provided in s 151(a)` (`a grant` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `paragraph (c)(1) of section 141 governs the corporation` `fixing the designations and preferences or rights of shares, or the number of shares of a series, or authorizing an increase or decrease in them, under a resolution adopted by the board as provided in s 151(a)` (`a grant` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Dividend, issuance of stock, s 253 certificate: only if the resolution, bylaws or certificate expressly so provide (and the power is given).
#ASSERT `s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `paragraph (c)(1) of section 141 governs the corporation` `declaring a dividend` (`a grant` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `paragraph (c)(1) of section 141 governs the corporation` `declaring a dividend` (`a grant` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `paragraph (c)(1) of section 141 governs the corporation` `declaring a dividend` (`a grant` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `paragraph (c)(1) of section 141 governs the corporation` `authorizing the issuance of stock` (`a grant` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `paragraph (c)(1) of section 141 governs the corporation` `authorizing the issuance of stock` (`a grant` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `paragraph (c)(1) of section 141 governs the corporation` `adopting a certificate of ownership and merger pursuant to s 253` (`a grant` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `paragraph (c)(1) of section 141 governs the corporation` `adopting a certificate of ownership and merger pursuant to s 253` (`a grant` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Every other matter (a merger under a section (c)(1) does not list; a matter submitted to stockholders): to the extent provided.
#ASSERT `s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `paragraph (c)(1) of section 141 governs the corporation` `adopting an agreement of merger or consolidation under a section other than those s 141(c)(1) lists` (`a grant` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `paragraph (c)(1) of section 141 governs the corporation` `any other matter in the management of the business and affairs of the corporation` (`a grant` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `paragraph (c)(1) of section 141 governs the corporation` `any other matter in the management of the business and affairs of the corporation` (`a grant` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `paragraph (c)(1) of section 141 governs the corporation` `approving or adopting, or recommending to the stockholders, an action or matter expressly required by this chapter to be submitted to stockholders for approval` (`a grant` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- (c)(2) src:366: no power to approve or recommend a matter required to be submitted to stockholders (other than the election or removal of directors), nor to adopt, amend or repeal a bylaw.
#ASSERT `s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `paragraph (c)(2) of section 141 governs the corporation` `approving or adopting, or recommending to the stockholders, an action or matter expressly required by this chapter to be submitted to stockholders for approval` (`a grant` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `paragraph (c)(2) of section 141 governs the corporation` `amending a bylaw of the corporation` (`a grant` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `paragraph (c)(2) of section 141 governs the corporation` `adopting a bylaw of the corporation` (`a grant` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `paragraph (c)(2) of section 141 governs the corporation` `repealing a bylaw of the corporation` (`a grant` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The election or removal of directors is carved out of the bar: to the extent provided.
#ASSERT `s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `paragraph (c)(2) of section 141 governs the corporation` `approving or recommending the election or removal of directors` (`a grant` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `paragraph (c)(2) of section 141 governs the corporation` `approving or recommending the election or removal of directors` (`a grant` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Under (c)(2) a dividend, an issuance of stock and a s 253 certificate need no express provision.
#ASSERT `s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `paragraph (c)(2) of section 141 governs the corporation` `declaring a dividend` (`a grant` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `paragraph (c)(2) of section 141 governs the corporation` `authorizing the issuance of stock` (`a grant` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `paragraph (c)(2) of section 141 governs the corporation` `adopting a certificate of ownership and merger pursuant to s 253` (`a grant` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A certificate amendment, a merger, a sale of assets, a dissolution: barred when this chapter submits it to stockholders; not otherwise.
#ASSERT `s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `paragraph (c)(2) of section 141 governs the corporation` `amending the certificate of incorporation, otherwise than by fixing the terms of shares under a resolution adopted as provided in s 151(a)` (`a grant` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `paragraph (c)(2) of section 141 governs the corporation` `adopting an agreement of merger or consolidation under s 251, 252, 254, 255, 256, 257, 258, 263 or 264` (`a grant` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `paragraph (c)(2) of section 141 governs the corporation` `any other matter in the management of the business and affairs of the corporation` (`a grant` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `paragraph (c)(2) of section 141 governs the corporation` `any other matter in the management of the business and affairs of the corporation` (`a grant` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Subcommittees`

-- src:367: a committee may create subcommittees unless the certificate, the bylaws or the board's resolution designating the committee provide otherwise.
#ASSERT `s 141(c)(3) the committee may create the subcommittee and delegate its powers to it` `in none of these` 2 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 141(c)(3) the committee may create the subcommittee and delegate its powers to it` `in the certificate of incorporation` 2 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 141(c)(3) the committee may create the subcommittee and delegate its powers to it` `in the bylaws` 2 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 141(c)(3) the committee may create the subcommittee and delegate its powers to it` `in a resolution of the board of directors` 2 TRUE
#ASSERT `s 141(c)(3) the committee may create the subcommittee and delegate its powers to it` `in none of these` 1 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 141(c)(3) the committee may create the subcommittee and delegate its powers to it` `in none of these` 0 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 141(c)(3) the committee may create the subcommittee and delegate its powers to it` `in none of these` 2 FALSE
-- src:367: a reference elsewhere in the chapter to a committee includes a subcommittee; a reference inside subsection (c) does not.
#ASSERT `s 141(c)(3) a reference to a committee includes a subcommittee` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 141(c)(3) a reference to a committee includes a subcommittee` TRUE

§ `The quorum and the act of a committee or subcommittee`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      q IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      wq IS A `s 141(c)(4) Where the committee's number is fixed`
      g IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      wg IS A `s 141(c)(4) Where the committee's number is fixed`
GIVETH A `s 141(c)(4) Committee provisions`
`a committee` n q wq g wg MEANS `s 141(c)(4) Committee provisions` WITH
    `the number of directors then serving on the committee or subcommittee` IS n
    `the number fixed as a quorum` IS q
    `where the quorum is fixed` IS wq
    `the number of members who must vote in favor, if a greater number is fixed` IS g
    `where the greater vote is fixed` IS wg

-- src:368: a majority of the 6 directors then serving is 4 (3 is half); no number fixed.
#ASSERT `s 141(c)(4) a quorum of the committee is present` 4 (`a committee` 6 NOTHING `in none of these, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)` NOTHING `in none of these, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 141(c)(4) a quorum of the committee is present` 3 (`a committee` 6 NOTHING `in none of these, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)` NOTHING `in none of these, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A lesser or greater number fixed in a recognised place; never below 1/3 of those serving (2 of 6 is exactly 1/3).
#ASSERT `s 141(c)(4) a quorum of the committee is present` 2 (`a committee` 6 (JUST 2) `in the bylaws, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)` NOTHING `in none of these, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 141(c)(4) a quorum of the committee is present` 1 (`a committee` 6 (JUST 2) `in the bylaws, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)` NOTHING `in none of these, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 141(c)(4) a quorum of the committee is present` 2 (`a committee` 6 (JUST 1) `in the bylaws, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)` NOTHING `in none of these, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 141(c)(4) a quorum of the committee is present` 5 (`a committee` 6 (JUST 5) `in a resolution of the committee that created the subcommittee, under s 141(c)(4)` NOTHING `in none of these, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 141(c)(4) a quorum of the committee is present` 4 (`a committee` 6 (JUST 5) `in a resolution of the committee that created the subcommittee, under s 141(c)(4)` NOTHING `in none of these, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 141(c)(4) a quorum of the committee is present` 4 (`a committee` 6 (JUST 5) `in a resolution of the board of directors, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)` NOTHING `in none of these, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 141(c)(4) a quorum of the committee is present` 4 (`a committee` 6 (JUST 5) `in the certificate of incorporation, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)` NOTHING `in none of these, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- More than the number serving cannot be a quorum: not covered. A number fixed nowhere is ignored: the majority of 4 stands.
#ASSERT `s 141(c)(4) a quorum of the committee is present` 4 (`a committee` 6 (JUST 7) `in the bylaws, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)` NOTHING `in none of these, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 141(c)(4) a quorum of the committee is present` 4 (`a committee` 6 (JUST 5) `in none of these, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)` NOTHING `in none of these, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 141(c)(4) a quorum of the committee is present` 1 (`a committee` 0 NOTHING `in none of these, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)` NOTHING `in none of these, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)`) EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:368: the act is the vote of the majority of the members present at a quorate meeting: 4 present, 3 is a majority, 2 is not.
#ASSERT `s 141(c)(4) the act of the committee is carried` 4 3 (`a committee` 6 NOTHING `in none of these, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)` NOTHING `in none of these, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 141(c)(4) the act of the committee is carried` 4 2 (`a committee` 6 NOTHING `in none of these, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)` NOTHING `in none of these, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 3 present is below the quorum of 4: no act.
#ASSERT `s 141(c)(4) the act of the committee is carried` 3 3 (`a committee` 6 NOTHING `in none of these, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)` NOTHING `in none of these, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A greater number fixed in the bylaws: 4 votes needed; 3 does not carry, 4 does. Ignored if fixed nowhere.
#ASSERT `s 141(c)(4) the act of the committee is carried` 5 3 (`a committee` 6 NOTHING `in none of these, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)` (JUST 4) `in the bylaws, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 141(c)(4) the act of the committee is carried` 5 4 (`a committee` 6 NOTHING `in none of these, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)` (JUST 4) `in the bylaws, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 141(c)(4) the act of the committee is carried` 5 3 (`a committee` 6 NOTHING `in none of these, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)` (JUST 4) `in none of these, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Where the quorum is not covered, nor is the act.
#ASSERT `s 141(c)(4) the act of the committee is carried` 5 4 (`a committee` 6 (JUST 7) `in the bylaws, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)` NOTHING `in none of these, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)`) EQUALS NOTHING
